1
00:00:00,039 --> 00:00:02,979
You're using Grok Bot wrong.

2
00:00:03,178 --> 00:00:05,398
Most people make it write code.

3
00:00:05,724 --> 00:00:09,344
The team that built it does the opposite.

4
00:00:09,856 --> 00:00:13,996
Their bots hand every coding
task to a cloud agent.

5
00:00:14,346 --> 00:00:17,206
With one rule: bring back proof.

6
00:00:17,302 --> 00:00:21,242
Screenshots and green
tests, or it goes back.

7
00:00:21,668 --> 00:00:26,848
One engineer went from juggling fifteen
agents to more than two hundred.

8
00:00:27,170 --> 00:00:31,050
Every night at three, the
bots audit the codebase.

9
00:00:31,256 --> 00:00:33,876
By eight, the PRs are waiting.

10
00:00:34,393 --> 00:00:37,807
So stop asking Grok Bot
to write your code.

11
00:00:37,827 --> 00:00:39,407
Ask it to run your loop.

12
00:00:39,507 --> 00:00:41,727
Full playbook on the channel.
